// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// DIAGNOSIS OF ATTEMPT 23 FAILURE (0% accuracy):
//
// ROOT CAUSE: Removing int() from guidance caused ALL 46 constrained examples to fail.
// Without int() instruction, the model generated bare variable names (n, price, usage)
// as constrained content. The parser accepts single identifiers as complete arithmetic
// expressions, so CloseSpanIfComplete fired after just 1 token: <<n>>, <<usage>>, <<1>>.
// Metrics confirm: avg visible span token length = 1.47, median = 1.00, 41/49 tiny spans.
// A bare variable never equals the correct multi-variable formula → 0% accuracy.
